<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bayreuth</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bayreuth is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-franconia">Upper Franconia</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Under the Franconian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a> it became in the early 17th century the residence of the margraves of Brandenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulmbach">Kulmbach</a>, thereafter called Brandenburg-Bayreuth, whose court built the Margravial Opera House, now a World Heritage Site. Since 1876 it has hosted the Bayreuth Festival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-wagner">Richard Wagner</a>'s operas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bayreuth.jpg" alt="Bayreuth" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Sander · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marktplatz_Bayreuth.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
